    {
      "id": "dsa5105-linear-week1-example-1",
      "type": "worked-example",
      "title": "Worked example: fit a line by hand",
      "steps": [
        "For x = {0, 1, 2} and y = {1, 2, 2}, the means are x-bar = 1 and y-bar = 5/3.",
        "The centered numerator is (-1)(-2/3) + 0(1/3) + (1)(1/3) = 1. The centered denominator is 1 + 0 + 1 = 2, so w1-hat = 1/2.",
        "The intercept is y-bar - w1-hat x-bar = 5/3 - 1/2 = 7/6. The fitted line is f-hat(x) = 7/6 + x/2."
      ],
      "answer": "OLS separates slope from intercept by centering first; check the denominator before dividing.",
