    {
      "id": "dsa5105-linear-week1-example-2",
      "type": "worked-example",
      "title": "Worked example: softmax to logistic",
      "steps": [
        "For two logits z1 and z2, subtract z2 from both logits without changing the probability ratio.",
        "Only s = z1 - z2 remains, giving p1 = 1/(1 + exp(-s)) and p2 = 1 - p1.",
        "With labels y in {-1, +1}, the cross-entropy can be written as log(1 + exp(-y s)); classify as class 1 when s is positive and class 2 when s is negative."
      ],
      "answer": "Binary logistic regression is the two-class softmax written in terms of one score difference.",
