    {
      "id": "dsa5105-linear-week1-example-3",
      "type": "worked-example",
      "title": "Worked example: when to reach for Huber",
      "steps": [
        "If most residuals are small but one measurement is far away, squared loss makes that point's contribution grow quadratically.",
        "Huber loss keeps the quadratic region near zero but switches to a linear contribution beyond delta.",
        "Use validation evidence to decide whether the robustness tradeoff improves the target metric; do not assume Huber is always better."
      ],
      "answer": "Huber changes the loss and therefore the optimization target; it is not a free outlier-removal step.",
